      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, some (but not all) of the registers are just inverted for some reason. \n\nAnd Keith, thats not exactly right (which proves your point that I need a comment). The CC line is used for both FRS detection and passthrough to the TCPC. So, when cc_polarity is 1, cc2 is cc (and used for FRS), and cc1 is vconn (so here we are cutting it off from the TCPC).",
